From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:20:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] DKIM2: an unsigned post leaves with one m=1, Recipe back
 to the original

A post that arrived without a DKIM2-Signature is no longer stripped of
its chain at egress.  Each copy leaves with a single Message-Instance,
m=1, carrying the hashes of the rewritten, decorated copy and a Recipe
back to the message as received: the original From in the header
Recipe, the wrap's copy range (or none/null as for any copy) in the body
Recipe.  -07 section 12.1 lets the first instance record the changes made
as the message enters DKIM2, and the From-Authentic check pairs i=1 with
the From of that first state, which is the rewritten one.  The instance
replaces the one(s) the message arrived with; if it cannot be calculated
the chain is removed and the outbound signer starts it.

egress_context marks such a context "unsigned"; egress_add calculates
against the saved header block as for any copy and numbers the result 1
(the hashes and Recipes do not cover Message-Instance fields).

Also: X-DKIM2-Exploded goes on every copy from a DKIM2 list, with or
without an egress context, and DoForward's From-rewrite shelving has a
test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
